course: dictionary
lesson: 1904
title: Colourful: bright or lively
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Colourful is an adjective, a describing word. It tells you about a noun, such as a fish, a picture or a story. It comes from colour with -ful added, so it means full of colour. «Koi are colourful carp bred in Japan» tells you the fish are full of bright colours.
explain: The word has a second meaning too: interesting, lively and exciting. A colourful character in a story is not painted with bright paint. The author means the character is lively and memorable. The words around the word give you the clue: is the writer talking about a picture, or about a person or a story?
explain: Use the swap check. Replace colourful with bright, or with lively and exciting, and see which one still makes sense. «Some koi have been reported to live for over a hundred years» does not need colourful at all, so the word is describing the fish, not the years.
fact: Colourful means having many bright colours.
fact: Colourful also means interesting, lively and exciting, as in a colourful character or a colourful story.
fact: Useful phrases: bright and colourful; a colourful character.
fact: In nature, parrots, flowers and coral reefs are colourful.
fact: In American English the word is spelled colorful, without the u.
exercise: «Koi are colourful carp bred in Japan.» What does colourful mean here? | Very quiet | Heavy to lift | *Having many bright colours | Dull and grey
exercise: Mia says a colourful character must be a painter. What does colourful mean in a colourful character? | Dull and plain | *Lively and interesting | A character who paints pictures | A character with no name
exercise: «The parrot had colourful feathers.» Find and copy the describing word. | parrot | had | *colourful | feathers
test: «The coral reef was colourful and full of fish.» What does colourful mean? | *Full of bright colours | Very old | Hidden under the sand | Cold and grey
test: «A colourful story keeps you reading.» What does colourful mean? | Dull and boring | Written in pencil | *Lively and exciting | Very short
exam: Which sentence uses colourful to mean lively and exciting? | The bus was yellow and parked | The paper was white and plain | The fish had colourful scales | *The teacher told a colourful story full of jokes and adventures
